# title: SOUL DUEL NEXT
# SOUL DUEL sources in compile order, relative to this directory (the engine's come first, see
# engine/MANIFEST). Order matters: macros, structs, components and special variables before their
# users. tuning / rules / control / kit are plain CL (host-tested); ken / ichigo / hisagi are the characters
# (data + hooks + cinematics); fighter ... main are the generic systems (no character names, except gate.lisp's pacing companions and debug.lisp's test scenarios).
# scripted.lisp (the trial player tools/simgate/trial.lisp drives) loads right before cpu-perceive.lisp (the CPUs' perception and presses).
# ken-meter (Kenpachi's Shikai :p and the meter's :label) loads right after hud.lisp.
# fq-online.lisp (the online fuzzy Q against a human: LEARNING CPU) loads after the CPUs it records (core-ai, cpu-mcts).
# hem-spring / tip-track / vfx-ember (shared looks that stayed when the retired kits left: Ichigo's cloak spring, the weapon-tip tracker Ichigo's and Kenpachi's looks use, the ember star and the hold charge the dispatch calls) load before the characters.
# hisagi.lisp, then hisagi-art / hisagi-draw / hisagi-cine / hisagi-stills (Hisagi, kit :hisagi, roster index 7,
# docs/duel/DUEL_HISAGI.md). The retired kits' files (Yamamoto, Rukia, Senjumaru, Lille) left on 2026-11-12: branch `retired-kits`; their
# roster slots are fixed in kit.lisp *ROSTER* (the roster is append-only). A character's files all carry its prefix (<name>.lisp the kit, <name>-ai the CPU, <name>-art
# the clips, <name>-draw / -cine / -stills by role).
